\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The untwisted signs agree with the counting convention}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{At trivial links, #{T_i^U} is the ordinary shift and its
inverse is the backward shift. The formulas in
[the paired construction](fdip-00SR) then read
#{\extD=\extd+\extdag} and #{\cov=\extd-\extdag}, the
same two choices distinguished in \ref{fdip-00PV}.
An alternating perfect coefficient form also permits the
algebraic adjoint calculation. It supplies no positive
quadratic norm for a Hodge argument.}
